Z||000000||JD86GT350||11-06-2001||07:26 PM||||Help!<P>I took the tilt column out of my '84 SE auto, and stuck in into my '86 GT stick.  I thought the auto interlock was just a mechanical do-dad that kept me from taking the key out, but now that the column is in the GT it won't start...acts just like there's a cut-off somewhere stopping it.<P>am I missing something?||||reg||4
Z||000001||fix||11-06-2001||07:37 PM||||Escanaba huh?  I'm go to Michigan Tech in Houghton, so you're about the closest person on this forum to me during the school year. <P>About the steering column, I don't think there is a difference other than that park/neutral safety switch.  I would just double check all the connections again. If that doesn't work, maybe someone else can clarify the differences in the columns.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||JD86GT350||11-06-2001||07:51 PM||||son of a!<P>I just stuck the stick column back in to see...<BR>same problem!<P>I messed something up...I wonder what!<BR>anybody got any pointers?||||reg||5
Z||000003||theogre||11-06-2001||07:56 PM||||The ignition switch has some adjustment where it bolts to the top of the column. If that's moved it could keep it from starting. beyond that it's hard to say without seeing it.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||JD86GT350||11-06-2001||08:03 PM||||shouldn't be the switch, I never touched it, these were whole column swaps, I was just gonna trade keys too, but now I get the same problem with the old column back in its original place, I must have tugged too hard on a wire....acts like its grounding out or something<P>EDIT:  just found two plastic clips on the floormat in the corner, hmmm, wonder if I screwed up the clutch switch...<p>[This message has been edited by JD86GT350 (edited 11-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||dcaprio||11-06-2001||11:16 PM||||Funny thing, I just put a stick column in my auto car. It worked out fine. Just a shot in the dark. Did you disconect the battery before installing the column ? If not check the fuses first. Then I would check to see if theres a switch on the clutch pedal. Some cars have such a switch to stop idiots from starting there car in gear. When I installed the stick column in my car I had a plug with 3 or 4 wires going to a black plug. I had no idea where it went but everything worked so I didn't give it much thought till now. That could have gone to the switch on the clutch. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||JD86GT350||11-07-2001||06:59 AM||||yeah, battery was disconnected.<BR>the more I think about it I'm leaning toward that clutch switch, when I got home and looked at my Haynes it looks like those two clips I found act as a collar on the neutral start switch.  Plus its acting just like that switch is to blame...<P>oh well, I'll dig into it again today||||reg||1
Z||000007||JD86GT350||11-07-2001||08:50 AM||||problem solved, I"m a big dummy!<P>of course those two clips are the collar for the neutral start switch!<P>for anybody wondering, this actually was really easy, and I would have been completed in about an hour had I been paying attention.<P>the GT rumbles once again||||reg||14
